<title>SWEDEN: POLL-Ericsson H1 pre-tax seen up 21 pct. [CORRECTED 15:23 GMT]</title>
<headline>POLL-Ericsson H1 pre-tax seen up 21 pct. [CORRECTED 15:23 GMT]</headline>
<dateline>STOCKHOLM 1997-07-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Swedish telecoms giant L.M. Ericsson AB will return a first half pre-tax profit totalling 5.11 billion crowns, a 21 percent increase on the 1996 first half period profit of 4.22 billion, according to a Reuters survey of 16 analysts.  </p>
<p>The forecasts ranged between 4.6 and 5.4 billion crowns.</p>
<p>First half turnover is seen rising by 33 (correcting percentage change) percent to 66.45 billion. Full-year turnover was seen rising to 157 billion crowns.</p>
<p>PRE-TAX PROFIT</p>
<p>(billions)   average     range</p>
<p>H1     1997    5.112    4.600-  5.400</p>
<p>Year   1997   12.926   12.100- 13.605</p>
<p>Year   1998   15.882   14.500- 16.990</p>
<p>TURNOVER</p>
<p>H1     1997   66.445   65.205- 67.295</p>
<p>Year   1997  157.038  151.000-164.400</p>
<p>Year   1998  187.671  177.880-204.000</p>
<p>EPS</p>
<p>(crowns)</p>
<p>Year   1997    8.95     8.30-9.66</p>
<p>Year   1998   10.97     9.90-12.01</p>
<p>-- Simon Haydon, Stockholm newsroom +46-8-700-1004</p>
